WEBVTT

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.180
This is my dream of that day.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:12.080
Mom, I'm hungry!

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.950
Okay, Misa-chan.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:17.820
What do you want, some cheesecake
or a pear tart?

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:21.950
A tart!

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:27.230
Got it. I'll make it now,
so wait just a second.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:30.210
Hurry! Hurry!

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:31.830
Okay.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.280
But,

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:38.450
I was about to do something that
I could never take back.

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:44.350
The Daemon, summoned and sealed in a
bottle by my mother, over a year's time,

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:47.010
had turned to Code...

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:49.770
<i>That which hails from a distant Layer,</i>

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:51.270
In an attempt to control it,

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:52.600
<i>yield to my will.</i>

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.440
I messed up.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:12.330
<i>That which hails from a distant
Layer, yield to my will.</i>

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:15.600
I did it!

00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:32.390
Mom!

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:33.780
Stay there!

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:55.990
Mom!

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.340
It's okay.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.630
It's not scary anymore.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:05.900
Mom!

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.490
Mom!

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:11.910
Mom!

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:10.770
After that amount of exertion,

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:14.030
given her lack of initial
physical strength,

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:18.090
she died while giving
birth to Soshiro.

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:20.900
Mom!

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:26.260
Thank you for choosing us
for your flight today.

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:29.530
We departed from Yamagata
and will arrive in Haneda.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:15.980
Numerous Windows Broken at Electronics Store,
Suspect Still On the Loose

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:21.590
Small Fire at Games Company, Cause Unknown
Will New Product's Release Be Delayed?

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:19.050
Lately, there have been
a lot of unsolved incidents

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:22.620
with people using Codes
for wrongdoing...

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.980
They're all little things
that you'd miss

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:28.520
if you hadn't been paying
close attention.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:33.110
The Daemon-summoning incident
that Yumiko stumbled upon...

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:39.140
Someone's definitely using computers
to perform magic.

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:41.870
On top of that,

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:45.120
they're getting more advanced,
like they're learning.

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:50.010
But who would do that and why?

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:53.260
An intruder?

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:05.480
Oh, Koyomi... I wonder
what she's doing.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:09.940
Clean the warehouse?

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:15.080
Yeah, we'd like to thank her for
all the help she's given me.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.120
Right?

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:17.660
Yeah.

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:20.830
I came here since
you guys asked,

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:25.170
but why do I have to
clean Misa's house?

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:28.400
I thought you were supposed
to be Morishita's backup.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:30.170
What does that even mean?

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:33.140
By the way, where is Misa?

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:34.250
I don't know.

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:37.350
She left to buy some meat
and hasn't come back.

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:40.310
Well, I imagine she'll
be back by dinner.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:44.850
Hey! Get your act together!

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:47.750
If you're just going to make
it messier, go back home!

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:52.190
Looks like dinner tonight
will be fun.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:56.210
Almost makes it worth my
getting on this flight...

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:00.300
I didn't really want to, though.

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:02.200
I had a feeling something
bad was going to happen.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:06.920
A group of black cats
crossed my path.

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:13.720
My brand-new high heels broke.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:16.930
I decided to get some coffee,

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.010
and something else
came out instead.

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:24.360
I hope nothing else happens.

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:28.190
Whoops.

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:46.430
The Daemon-summoning Code
that Yumiko brought to me...

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:52.510
It's a modified version of the worm
I made a long time ago.

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:55.600
That's the Christmas Shopper?

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:57.030
Yes.

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:04.980
On Christmas Eve, this virus makes all
the idle computers around the world

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:10.890
start up on their own and play "Daisy
Daisy" for several seconds.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:19.820
New Virus Strikes on Christmas Eve!
Largest Number of Infected Systems Ever!

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:23.580
The total number of infected PCs
is said to be four or five million.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:25.550
Wow. That many?

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:33.580
The Christmas Shopper was quite the large magical
ceremony, creating a single magical item.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:41.210
But, something of that scale was
required to make a simple stone

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:44.100
into an amulet embedded
with 2048 variable Codes.

00:07:45.530 --> 00:07:49.270
I guess the police suspected
me thanks to that...

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:52.350
You did it!

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:54.840
Using someone's computer
without permission

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:58.530
is considered damage to electronic systems
and obstruction of business!

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:01.370
Hey, I wouldn't do something
like that.

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:04.490
Are you sure you're not
hiding something?

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:08.200
If you bring me some katsudon,

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:09.950
I might remember something.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:13.120
Well, I don't really mind,

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:14.460
but you're paying.

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:18.320
Didn't Detective Friday
say he'd get me some-

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:21.350
Who's Detective Friday? You've been
watching too many dramas!

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:23.770
I'm disappointed.

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:34.720
You're Anehara Misa, aren't you?

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:36.850
Who are you?

00:08:36.850 --> 00:08:40.050
Nice to meet you.
I'm Gary Huang.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:45.200
Like yourself, I'm a person of interest
in the Christmas Shopper case.

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:51.360
Sorry for having you
get me something.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:52.660
Not a problem.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.990
In any event, we're both
pretty unlucky.

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:59.190
Who would have thought they would
go and interrogate people?

00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:00.980
They're just going around,

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:05.190
grabbing any talented programmers
they can find.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:08.830
I bet they don't even have
a clue who it is.

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:15.470
Huang was a student from Hong Kong, studying
abroad, and a really talented programmer.

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:19.860
I thought he'd know who created
the Daemon-summoning Code

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:24.730
since he's offered to help
with a lot of cases, but...

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:28.580
This is probably Jinzai
Tsukumo's work.

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:36.030
Jinzai Tsukumo...

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:38.890
An e-mail?

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:44.710
"Hello! Are you enjoying
your smooth flight?"

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:47.980
"I know it's sudden, but I have something
important to tell you."

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:51.400
"On the plane you're on there's actually...

00:09:52.010 --> 00:09:53.410
a bomb"?

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:57.340
That's kind of an unnerving joke.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:10:00.000
And they seem to know
what I'm doing.

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:12.910
The source of the transmission
is moving...

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:16.020
I guess I'll stop them first.

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:29.890
Who are you?

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:34.610
Oh, I was noticed?

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:36.470
One New E-mail

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:45.140
<b>Boom</b>

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:40.450
"Are you sure you have
time to take me on?"

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:45.160
"If you don't hurry and find
the bomb, it'll explode!"

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:47.480
A bomb, huh?

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:51.680
That's quite the pickle...

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:52.810
Good luck today.

00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:53.650
My.

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:09.510
I guess I can't just let it go.

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:13.780
Looks like that bad
feeling was right.

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:24.790
We're done!

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:30.800
It's all clean now.

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:33.170
Well, it wasn't that bad.

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:34.280
Yeah!

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:44.840
Done here, too.

00:11:45.620 --> 00:11:46.810
Wow!

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:49.410
All the junk is out of sight.

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:51.620
Yeah, we went through a lot.

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:55.610
Tell Misa to stop buying
so much stuff.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:58.600
I tell her that all the time,
but she doesn't listen.

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:02.280
You guys want some
dinner, right?

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:04.650
I'm going shopping.
What do you want?

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:08.000
Hm, how about a stew?

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:09.960
Peking duck.

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:13.790
I feel like having some
black pudding.

00:12:15.090 --> 00:12:18.170
At least agree on
the type of food.

00:12:22.780 --> 00:12:24.830
It's not here...

00:12:24.830 --> 00:12:29.510
Well, I doubt they'd put it
in such an easy place.

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:30.930
Is something the matter?

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:33.280
Oh, nothing.

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:34.850
Don't worry about it.

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:42.370
I couldn't really ask her to look
for the bomb with me.

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:45.490
If I can't ask a person for help,

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:49.010
I guess I can ask the jini
living in the electronics.

00:12:52.780 --> 00:12:57.200
jini, do you see any signs that something
suspicious was snuck in here?

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:01.000
No, ma'am!

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:04.250
No, ma'am!

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:06.020
No, ma'am!

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:11.750
All clear, then...

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:15.200
Nothing here.

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:24.570
Nothing wrong here, either.

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:38.800
Mama, there's someone outside!

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:41.490
That's nice.

00:13:56.170 --> 00:13:58.630
Nothing to be found...

00:13:59.030 --> 00:14:02.410
Was something strange
really snuck in here?

00:14:02.410 --> 00:14:03.850
Yes, ma'am!

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:10.450
I wanted the search to end
with Jinzai Tsukumo.

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:21.390
Jinzai went missing
a few months ago.

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:27.630
He's not really dead, is he?

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:49.570
This is...

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:04.590
Found it!

00:15:08.070 --> 00:15:12.050
Having confirmed that Jinzai was the
author of the summoning Code,

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:15.240
I snuck around in a government
office's database,

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:17.860
and I found his parents' address.

00:15:19.990 --> 00:15:25.100
You really were alive,
Jinzai Tsukumo-san.

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:30.110
There's something I want to ask you
regarding the Code you created.

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:33.300
A long time ago,

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:35.940
when I first saw the
Christmas Shopper,

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:40.370
I thought to myself that I wanted
to write a similar program.

00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:47.410
I reverse assembled the executable I stumbled
across, researching it for months.

00:15:48.070 --> 00:15:52.900
I was really excited when
I finally got somewhere.

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:56.630
Then why are you hiding
in a place like this?

00:15:57.110 --> 00:15:59.390
That's because...

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:02.630
It was completely different
than what I'd imagined.

00:16:04.780 --> 00:16:07.340
With digital calculations,

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:09.820
if you give a system a bad order,

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:13.940
the system will carry out those
bad instructions to the letter.

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:18.850
But I couldn't control
that program at all!

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:23.170
I didn't even have a clue
as to how to control it.

00:16:24.510 --> 00:16:26.640
It wasn't science at all.

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:32.850
I got scared, destroyed everything,
and ran back here!

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:35.060
I see.

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:39.990
So you're not the one who
summoned the Daemons.

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:42.490
What are you talking about?

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:48.060
The Code you said you
destroyed is still alive.

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:52.130
I don't know! It wasn't me!

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:55.110
I have nothing to do with it
anymore! Leave me alone!

00:17:00.050 --> 00:17:04.630
Who's using Jinzai's Code?

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:14.500
This is...

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:22.440
Was it really necessary that
we all go shopping?

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:26.180
But thanks to that, we got
tons of eggs, vegetables,

00:17:26.180 --> 00:17:28.190
and other things limited
to one per customer.

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:31.230
Because someone here
likes to eat a lot,

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:32.700
my wallet thanks you.

00:17:33.730 --> 00:17:34.960
Who's that?

00:17:39.110 --> 00:17:41.440
That's mean!

00:17:51.390 --> 00:17:53.930
This is pretty suspicious.

00:17:53.930 --> 00:17:57.260
How did they get it in here, considering
everything that's been going on?

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:06.460
Here we go!

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:11.670
A jack-in-the-box?

00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:14.220
Damn it!

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:23.100
So he just wanted to distract me?

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:25.980
What a lot of trouble
for a simple theft...

00:18:27.760 --> 00:18:28.950
What's going on?

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:32.500
I don't know! It seems like all electronic
systems just went down.

00:18:33.660 --> 00:18:35.520
The APU won't start, either!

00:18:43.150 --> 00:18:45.960
A fake bomb and then
a blackout...

00:18:45.960 --> 00:18:47.850
He sure was cautious.

00:18:53.140 --> 00:18:54.380
Mr. Bear!

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:04.630
It's okay.

00:19:04.630 --> 00:19:06.020
It's not scary anymore.

00:19:07.050 --> 00:19:09.670
I'm borrowing your
bear for just a bit.

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:13.690
It'd suck to crash.

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:16.560
And I have some hungry
kids waiting for me,

00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:19.240
so I have to get home on time.

00:19:23.860 --> 00:19:24.970
My cell!

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:27.350
I thought I turned it off.

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:40.700
We're going to crash!

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:46.490
Clear the runway! Do it now!

00:19:46.730 --> 00:19:48.390
Have emergency vehicles
standing by!

00:19:48.390 --> 00:19:50.080
Prepare to put out any fires!

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:02.460
It's Mr. Bear!

00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:08.240
Thank goodness!

00:21:12.490 --> 00:21:14.020
Mr. Bear!

00:21:19.970 --> 00:21:22.830
Home is where the heart is...

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:25.690
This meat is really good!

00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:29.890
It is! Yonezawa beef is the best.

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:35.330
But how many hours did you
spend buying that meat?

00:21:35.570 --> 00:21:40.280
But, on the way, I saved a plane
that was going to crash.

00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:42.340
It was a lot of work!

00:21:42.340 --> 00:21:45.650
All you do is say these
ridiculous things.

00:21:45.650 --> 00:21:48.350
But it's true.

00:22:03.390 --> 00:22:09.640
I guess you really do need a mage if you're
going to take on another mage.

00:23:46.260 --> 00:23:48.620
An evil mage revives,

00:23:48.620 --> 00:23:54.790
and a Modern-Day mage and a Classical Mage
fight with both their lives on the line.

00:23:54.790 --> 00:23:58.590
Gary Huang's plan now
begins to move.

00:24:04.590 --> 00:24:07.090
Spell  =  Code?   Part 3

00:24:07.090 --> 00:24:14.170
Yamagata Airport?

00:24:08.250 --> 00:24:10.020
How did you enjoy Obon?

00:24:10.020 --> 00:24:11.530
Morishita Koyomi here!

00:24:11.530 --> 00:24:13.590
Let's have fun studying this week.

00:24:13.590 --> 00:24:15.210
Anehara Misa here.

00:24:15.210 --> 00:24:19.610
Last time, we studied Classical
Magic and its Codes,

00:24:19.610 --> 00:24:23.540
but this time, we're going to study
Modern-Day Magic and its Codes.

00:24:23.540 --> 00:24:25.040
Okay!

00:24:25.040 --> 00:24:29.480
Modern-Day Magic uses computers
to create magic, right?

00:24:28.510 --> 00:24:35.510
Haneda Airport

00:24:29.480 --> 00:24:31.500
Not just computers.

00:24:31.500 --> 00:24:35.660
As long as it's a machine that can run
a program, you can use it there, too.

00:24:35.660 --> 00:24:38.580
Th-There it is... Y-You
said, "program."

00:24:38.580 --> 00:24:42.260
Hey, remember things
already, Koyomi.

00:24:42.260 --> 00:24:45.880
B-But computers have
a lot of buttons!

00:24:45.880 --> 00:24:48.230
Of course they do. Jeez.

00:24:48.230 --> 00:24:49.540
I'm sorry.

00:24:49.540 --> 00:24:52.030
Okay, I'm going to keep on going.

00:24:51.010 --> 00:26:10.040
Modern-Day Magic and Codes

00:24:52.030 --> 00:24:54.860
Modern-Day Magic is different
from Classical Magic

00:24:54.860 --> 00:24:57.430
because it uses machines
in place of the body.

00:24:57.430 --> 00:25:00.860
So, you construct a Code via
a programming language,

00:25:00.860 --> 00:25:05.430
and magic results when a machine
processes that Code.

00:25:05.430 --> 00:25:07.000
I see. I see.

00:25:07.000 --> 00:25:09.940
Modern-Day Magic, unlike
Classical Magic,

00:25:09.940 --> 00:25:13.240
is independent of a person's
stamina or mental will,

00:25:09.940 --> 00:25:37.510
Not dependent on stamina or mental willpower.

00:25:13.240 --> 00:25:20.330
and Modern-Day Magic can work with the same
Code repeatedly until a given machine breaks.

00:25:20.580 --> 00:25:24.680
You can do simple things, but
as opposed to Classical Magic,

00:25:24.680 --> 00:25:29.420
you can't use a human's complex body
to reassemble Code while casting

00:25:27.330 --> 00:25:37.510
Difficult to reassemble Code

00:25:27.330 --> 00:25:37.510
based on a given situation.

00:25:29.420 --> 00:25:33.760
or construct complex Codes
based on a given situation.

00:25:33.760 --> 00:25:35.800
So basically,

00:25:35.800 --> 00:25:38.970
it's like comparing mass-produced
snacks and candies

00:25:38.300 --> 00:26:10.040
Modern-Day Magic

00:25:38.970 --> 00:25:43.530
